  "content": {
    "id": "v2-db8d2-p31-practice-slot-3-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Priya deposits $\\$900$ at the beginning of each quarter for 5 years into an account earning 6% p.a., compounded quarterly. Find the value of her investment at the end of the 5 years. Give your answer to the nearest cent.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\$21\\,123.47$",
      "worked": "Quarterly growth factor:\n$$r=1+\\frac{0.06}{4}=1.015.$$\nNumber of deposits: $n=5\\times4=20$.\n\nPayments are made at the beginning of each quarter.\n\nAfter 1 quarter: $900r$.\n\nAfter 2 quarters: $900r^2+900r$.\n\nAfter 20 quarters: $900r^{20}+900r^{19}+\\cdots+900r$.\n\nThis is a geometric series with $a=900r$, $r=1.015$ and $n=20$.\n$$\\begin{align*}FV&=\\frac{900(1.015)(1.015^{20}-1)}{0.015}\\\\FV&\\approx\\$21\\,123.47\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
